@@ -91,3 +91,12 @@ cleanup. Default `false` retains the existing best-effort behavior. Use a truste
 hook that durably copies declared evidence outside the workspace and verifies its
 checksums before success. Failure retains the workspace; repair the cause and
 retry cleanup. Startup/reload uses the same policy.
+
+### Local validation before GitHub publication
+
+A GitHub workflow may configure `tracker.provider.publication_guard` with an
+absolute host executable. This advertises `local_gate` (start/status) and requires
+a complete host validation receipt before agent ref or PR publication. The guard
+receives the controller-assigned issue and GitHub-resolved commit tree. Direct
+contents writes, force updates and alternate publication routes are rejected.
+The guard does not replace protected CI checks or alter lifecycle budgets.
